/*  thiele02_prater_temperature -- THE SINGLE CATALYST PELLET.

    What the student SEES:

      * the intraparticle CONCENTRATION FIELD c(r)/c_s from the pellet centre
        to its external surface, solved NUMERICALLY (central differences on the
        existing Newton + LU) and printed beside the CLOSED FORM at every node;
      * the EFFECTIVENESS FACTOR eta, computed twice by two independent
        functionals of the same field (the volume integral, and the surface
        gradient) and compared with the analytical eta;
      * the THIELE MODULUS in both of its conventions -- phi_char on the pellet
        radius, and the generalised phi on Lambda = V_p/S_p = R/3;
      * the classical eta(phi) FAMILY over all three geometries;
      * an ORDER-OF-CONVERGENCE study: the deviation from the closed form falls
        as h^2, which says the scheme is the one it claims to be rather than
        merely close on one grid.

    Read the README before quoting any number: the PELLET is a teaching
    surrogate and says so in its own record.  What this case verifies is the
    NUMERICS against the closed form, and that claim is independent of the
    surrogate's values.                                                        */

application   choupoProps;
description   "Single catalyst pellet: intraparticle concentration field, effectiveness factor, and the eta(phi) family, each verified against the first-order isothermal closed form";
verbosity     3;
